From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Suno <engineering@projectSuno.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:10:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] App icons: the plate fills the tile; icons without one get a
 drawn plate

A v4 Suno app icon draws its plate as a rounded square, 860 on its 1024
canvas, inside a transparent margin, so at a tile's size its plate was 84%
as large as the tile and the tile's corner mask never reached it. The
SunoUI app-icon helper (SunoAppIconPlate.js, used through iconMask.js
syncAppIconPlate) reads an icon's SVG once per file and modification time;
an icon whose first drawn element is a rounded square centred on a square
canvas has its texture rendered at least that large and is scaled about
its centre so the square meets the tile's edges exactly, and the tile
clips the margin. Any other icon, a raster, a legacy or third-party icon, or a file
that cannot be read, is drawn at the tile's size on a plate the Shell
draws behind it, never cropped.

The notification tile clips and masks its art as one actor so the icon can
be larger than the tile, and the app badge is a ring around a 16 px clip so
its icon never paints over the ring.
